<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-indices-standard-form" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Indices, Standard Form, and Estimation</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Index notation is a compact way to write repeated multiplication.
      Standard form extends this to represent very large and very small numbers.
      Estimation gives us the ability to work efficiently and check that answers are sensible.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="num_indices.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="num_standard-form.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="num_estimation.ptx" />

</chapter>
